  "task": {
    "objective": "Keep four kitchens serving their own changing festival orders by transporting food through distinct equipment stages, protecting heat, fueling the shared boiler and returning reusable trays through hands or a finite routed conveyor.",
    "natural_termination": "No natural success or joint-failure terminal. This is a continuing finite world. H=384 truncates the observation window, not a success event; done inputs are absorbing.",
    "interaction": "A dish requires different equipment in four locations. Route switches and occupancy change another kitchen's item delay and freshness. Plating removes a shared clean tray until a served or expired dish's dirty tray is washed and returned. Physical reports reveal another kitchen's order for a limited time; insulated porter tools alter hot-food transport timing and can be exchanged.",
    "observation_access": "The map, all physical staff cargo, stations, belt occupancy/direction, fuel/water levels, service clocks, public events and reward components are public. Current order flavour is directly visible only to the four actors belonging to that kitchen: order_visible is the kitchen-equality mask. Each observation adds only that actor's own notes and note_life rows. Speaking transfers the speaker's current home order to adjacent actors; foreign notes expire and can disagree with a changed live order. Legal serving masks do not test hidden flavour equality. A full-state/debug view must be labelled separately."
  },
